At the foot of Le Morne Brabant near the public beach the Slave Route Monument honours the maroons who escaped slavery and sought refuge on the mountain and all those enslaved in Mauritius.

The memorial bears lines from the poem *Le Morne Territoire Marron* by Richard Sedley Assonne. It remembers those who according to tradition "chose the kiss of death over the chains of slavery".

The monument is part of the Le Morne Cultural Landscape which has been a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 2008. Commemorations are held at Le Morne on 1 February for the anniversary of the abolition of slavery in Mauritius.

## Good to know

- This is a place of remembrance not a photo backdrop: please behave accordingly.
